 "text": "Under subsection 26(2) of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord is permitted to enter a rental unit without written notice between the hours of 8 a.m. and 8 p.m. if the tenancy agreement requires the landlord to clean the unit at regular intervals and the entry complies with the terms of that agreement. Because the clause specifies that the landlord will clean the unit weekly and enter for that purpose within the statutorily permitted hours, it is valid and enforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 26",
